  "result": {
    "summary": "Verified against packet vf34f9d2c01a0: _shadow_tool_disclosure correctly gates the specialist allowlist on both tool_disclosure==active and skill_routing==active (refusal already collapses skill mode to shadow via _prepare_skills, so the fallback to minimal is automatic and covered by test_skill_refusal_falls_back_to_minimal_allowlist). Mandatory tools are retained and unavailable/unknown tools are never added (specialist.compose already excludes them; this diff only wires the allowlist through). The needs_tool escalation path is untouched and still uses TOOLS[role] with the remaining budget/timeout (confirmed by test_escalation_still_uses_legacy_allowlist_under_hand_over). packet_meta and the tool_disclosure decision row record tool_allowlist_source (specialist/minimal/legacy/codex) and, on hand-over, reason 'specialist hand-over' plus tools_added/skills, matching the spec. Ran all four acceptance tests plus the full tests/test_spawn.py suite (121 tests) \u2014 all green. Docs in 08-specialists.md and 06-tool-disclosure.md accurately describe the new behavior and revert path. No issues found.",
